# Adoption checklist

Use this to roll out guardrails in **any** repo:

## Phase A — Document policy (week 1)

- [ ] Single coding standards doc (KISS, naming, errors, config)
- [ ] Durable **folder-structure blueprint** (principles, path map, placement, naming) — [`folder-structure`](./folder-structure.mdc) · [`../references/engineering/folder-structure.md`](../references/engineering/folder-structure.md)
- [ ] Security tier list + authorization rules
- [ ] Testing pyramid + naming
- [ ] Review severity tags defined
- [ ] Agent rules mirror docs (if using AI assistants)

## Phase B — Lint visibility (weeks 2–3)

- [ ] Run `/setup-skills` § Lint & format — prefer **Oxlint + Oxfmt** from [`references/lint/`](../references/lint/README.md)
- [ ] Migrating ESLint / Prettier / Biome? → `/migrate-oxlint` · `/migrate-oxfmt`
- [ ] Enable strict rules at `warn` globally
- [ ] Measure warning count per package
- [ ] Split shared preset modules (one concern each) when using ESLint modular presets
- [ ] Pre-commit on staged files (lefthook + lint-staged; stricter than global)
- [ ] Scoped lint/format documented in `docs/agents/lint.md`

## Phase C — Diff ratchet (weeks 4–5)

- [ ] CI job: lint changed files vs merge-base
- [ ] Layer 1: block new violations + count increases
- [ ] Layer 2: boy-scout K with waiver escape hatch
- [ ] Playbook for merge hygiene
- [ ] Local run script with `BASE_REF` / `HEAD_REF`

## Phase D — Custom validators (weeks 6–8)

- [ ] File suffix or module boundary checker (if applicable)
- [ ] Folder-placement / structure check against the blueprint (if applicable)
- [ ] Config-literal scanner on added lines
- [ ] Unit tests for classifiers
- [ ] `ci:*` local aliases

## Phase E — Contract mode (weeks 7–9)

- [ ] Team has read [`contract-format`](../references/spec/contract-format.md) (§G §C §I §R §V §T §B + ownership + right-size)
- [ ] Active `SPEC.md` uses that schema (concise; no prose-only contracts)
- [ ] contract / build / contract-check / contract-backprop (+ grill / research / code-review / codebase-design as reach-for)
- [ ] Right-size: typo → build only; high blast → grill + code-review first
- [ ] Backprop protocol on test failure (§B + prefer new §V)
- [ ] One pilot feature end-to-end through the chain (main thread — no sub-agents for the core loop)

## Phase F — Agent workflows

- [ ] Repo-root `AGENTS.md` from [`agents-root-template`](../references/pack/agents-root-template.md) — bootstrap, repo map, commands, learned facts
- [ ] `.cursor/rules/` — all pack `*.mdc` installed and always-on
- [ ] Skills under `.cursor/skills/<slug>/` (no parallel skill tree)
- [ ] `/ship` orchestrator at `.cursor/commands/ship.md` + JSON run state
- [ ] `.cursor/agents/` — subagent presets installed; delegation policy read
- [ ] Compressed subagent output contracts honored (parent paraphrases for humans)
- [ ] Run directory + resume semantics exercised once
- [ ] Concise communication enabled for long sessions
- [ ] Env branches + Release Please path documented (`dev`/`staging`/`main`) — [`release-lifecycle`](../references/ship/release-lifecycle.md); rebase-and-merge into `dev`

## Phase G — Promote warn → error (ongoing)

- [ ] Per-package promotion when warning count hits zero for N weeks
- [ ] Track in engineering metrics / burn-down board

